      "side": 1,
      "message": "Before the code change, it appears like we would short-circuit and drop the receiver if there is a \"Stop\" message. \nWith the code change, even after `stop` is called, it could be possible that existence of some previously-obtained senders may cause the receiver to never return an error in this loop.\nShould we add a check at L231 to check whether or not `GLOBAL_MODULE_RUNNER` is still running before calling `send`?",
